1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Introduction and Purpose

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Introduction and Purpose

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Hello, everyone!

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Do you want to play in VRChat wearing garments you've personally designed?

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Create unique avatars with your own special designs.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
It's easy with everywhere!

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In this video, we will learn how to convert garments from Clo or Marvelous Designer into VRChat garments using Everywhere.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:42,000
VRChat is a Metverse platform that allows users to create 3D avatars, interact with other users, and engage in various real-life experiences and games.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:51,000
In this tutorial, we'll learn how to create VRChat garments using Everywhere, Vroid Studio, Blender, and Unity.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Before we dive into VRChat,

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
if you haven't gone through the basic tutorial of Everywhere,

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
we recommend you to learn the fundamentals first before proceeding with this tutorial.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Please refer to the link provided at the top or in the description.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
VRChat Rule Guide

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
To create items in VRChat, there are certain rules you need to follow.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The production rules are separated based on PC and Android platforms.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
For PC,

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,000
the mesh limit is 70,000, with a recommended mesh count of 32,000.

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The maximum number of materials is 32, with a recommended count of 4.

20
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
In this tutorial, we will focus on creating avatars and garments based on the PC version.

21
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
You may find more detailed guidelines at the provided link.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Creating Avatar in Vroid Studio

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Now, let's create an avatar for VRChat using Vroid Studio.

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Vroid Studio is a free avatar creation tool provided by Pixiv,

25
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
allowing easy customization of Vroid avatars.

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Please access the link provided at the top to download and install Vroid Studio.

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Once installation is complete and Vroid Studio is opened,

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
click Create New and choose the desired gender for your avatar.

29
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
To dress your avatar in the created garments,

30
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
you'll need an avatar without clothes.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
To remove default clothing,

32
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
click on the Outfit tab at the top,

33
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
and delete the clothing from the top and bottom menus.

34
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
If you wish to wear specific shoes and socks,

35
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
please select and equip them accordingly.

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
You can customize your avatar's face and hairstyle under the Face and Hairstyle tabs at the top.

37
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Be cautious not to make your avatar excessively large or elaborate,

38
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
as it may increase the polygon count.

39
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Save the created avatar for future use or modifications.

40
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Click on the Menu button at the top right,

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
then click Save As to save the file in Vroid format.

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Once your avatar is fully configured,

43
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
export it.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Click on the icon at the top right,

45
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
then select Export as VRM.

46
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
A window will open for setting export options.

47
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Set Reduce Polygons for the body to 34

48
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
and Reduce Materials for Materials to 2.

49
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Then, click the Export button.

50
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
When the VRM Settings window appears,

51
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
fill in the information,

52
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
select VRM 0.0,

53
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
enter the title and creator details,

54
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
and click the Export button at the bottom.

55
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Please specify the saving path to save the VRM file.

56
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Avatar Format Conversion in Blender

57
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Blender Installation

58
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Please download the file from the link above to install Blender.

59
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
For this tutorial, we will use Blender 3.0.1.

60
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Installing the CATS plugin

61
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,000
To utilize Vroid avatars for 3D garments in Blender,

62
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
you need to convert the file format.

63
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
We'll utilize the CATS plugin,

64
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
as it's necessary for this format conversion process.

65
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Please go to the link provided at the top to download the plugin

66
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
and follow the guide to install it in Blender.

67
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Go to the top menu,

68
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Edit,

69
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Preferences,

70
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Add-ons,

71
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
click the Install button

72
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
and open the downloaded file.

73
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Check the installed CATS Blender plugin to activate its features.

74
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
VRM to FBX Conversion

75
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Once the plugin is installed,

76
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
click on the newly added CATS tab on the right side.

77
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Select Import Model, VRM

78
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:24,000
and choose the avatar file in VRM format that you want to import.

79
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
In the import window, select the option

80
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Extract Texture Images into the Folder

81
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
on the right side to import.

82
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Click on the icon next to Fix Model in the CATS add-on.

83
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Select the same options as shown on the screen,

84
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
then click OK and Fix Model.

85
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Once the fix model process is completed,

86
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
switch to pose mode to test

87
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:05,000
if the model has been corrected without any issues.

88
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
If everything looks fine,

89
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
exit the pose mode and click on Export Model.

90
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Click Continue to export in the warning dialog

91
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
and save it as an FBX file.

92
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:27,000
We'll import this FBX file as an avatar into Marvelous Designer

93
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
and then dress the outfit on it.

94
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Once you've finished creating the outfit,

95
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
you'll likely want to save the avatar file process

96
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
with Fix Model in Blender format.

97
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
This will be necessary for both the outfit

98
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
and avatar organization processes later on.

99
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Garment Conversion in Everywhere

100
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Now, let's create VRChat garments

101
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
using everywhere in the following order.

102
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Auto-fitting,

103
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Rigging,

104
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
UV Packing,

105
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Texture Baking,

106
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
and Uplift.

107
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Everywhere offers the same functionalities

108
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
within Clow and Marvelous Designer,

109
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
so it's recommended to use your preferred software.

110
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Downloading Garments from Connect

111
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,000
The garments for the tutorial are available on Connect.

112
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Click on the link at the top to access Connect.

113
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Add the garments to your cart,

114
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
proceed with the purchase,

115
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:36,000
and then download the files.

116
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Open the downloaded garment file in Marvelous Designer

117
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:49,000
and import the FBX avatar file from Blender.

118
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Click on the link at the top to access the FBX avatar file.

119
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Click on the link at the top to access the FBX avatar file.

120
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Auto-fitting

121
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
If the avatar's size has been changed in Vroid Studio

122
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
and the garments no longer fit properly,

123
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
we recommend using the auto-fitting feature.

124
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Auto-fitting automatically adjusts and fits patterns

125
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
to match the size of the avatar.

126
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
For a detailed tutorial on auto-fitting,

127
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
please refer to the link above.

128
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
The garments provided by Connect

129
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
are fitted to the default size,

130
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
so we will skip the auto-fitting process

131
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
and directly dress the outfit and avatar.

132
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Rigging

133
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Now, let's open Everywhere

134
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
and proceed with polygon optimization and rigging.

135
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
As the first step,

136
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
let's optimize the polygons

137
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,000
based on the polycount standards required by VRChat.

138
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:46,000
The polygon count for a single garment

139
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
including the avatar

140
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,000
should not exceed 70,000.

141
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Please adjust the mesh count accordingly,

142
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
keeping some room for flexibility.

143
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Enter the numbers and click Optimize.

144
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Once optimization is done,

145
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
simulate the garment again.

146
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Next, click on Apply

147
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
for rigging to start auto-rigging.

148
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Once rigging is complete,

149
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
click on the brush icon to open the brush window.

150
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Use the weight brush to make adjustments to the weights.

151
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Before getting into weight modification,

152
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
change the pose and identify areas

153
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
where you need to adjust weights.

154
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Adjust the blend mode and properties of the brush

155
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
while making modifications.

156
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Use the sculpt brush to smooth out surfaces

157
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
or refine shapes.

158
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Once rigging adjustments are done,

159
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
press the exit button to close the brush window.

160
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
UV Packing and Texture Baking

161
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Now the rigging is complete,

162
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
let's switch to the Material tab

163
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
in the Everywhere window to work on the textures.

164
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Before packing UVs,

165
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
you need to set the image size.

166
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Choose your desired image size in the options.

167
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Please avoid selecting too large sizes

168
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
due to texture size limitations.

169
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Once image and seam size configurations are done,

170
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
click the Pack UVs button.

171
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Set the packing ratio value,

172
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
choose other options if necessary,

173
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
and then press the Apply button to pack.

174
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Once UV packing is complete,

175
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,000
click the Close button to return to the Material tab.

176
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
After checking the maps you want to generate

177
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
in Texture Baking,

178
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
press the Apply button.

179
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
We will keep the default settings.

180
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Once baking is complete,

181
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
you can check the generated Normal map

182
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
and Ambient Occlusion map.

183
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
After texture baking is complete,

184
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
a corresponding number of materials

185
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,000
will be generated in the material list below

186
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
based on the number of UV tiles.

187
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
If you wish to have different materials

188
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
for each part in Unity,

189
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
please separate the materials.

190
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
However, for this tutorial,

191
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
we will not separate the material

192
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
and will proceed using one material.

193
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Upload

194
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
When the garment creation is finished,

195
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
click the Upload button

196
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
to open the Export Options window.

197
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Since we only need the garment,

198
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
please do not select the avatar.

199
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Choose the necessary textures

200
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
from the options below.

201
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Click OK to upload to connect.

202
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Access Connect and download the FBX file.

203
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
When you open the zip file,

204
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
you will find the FBX file

205
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
along with the texture map files.

206
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Organizing Custom Model in Blender

207
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
To upload items to VRChat,

208
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
integration of the avatar and garment,

209
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
deletion of hidden parts of the body mesh,

210
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
since Everywhere doesn't currently

211
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
provide these features,

212
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
we'll proceed with these tasks in Blender.

213
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Import FBX and Fix Model

214
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Open the Blender file of the avatar

215
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
that you saved in the previous

216
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
format conversion process.

217
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
In the top menu bar,

218
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
click File, Import,

219
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
FBX to open the garment FBX file

220
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
downloaded from Connect.

221
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Keep the file settings on the right unchanged

222
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
and import it as is.

223
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Delete the collection in the Scene Collection

224
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
on the top right.

225
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
On the top right in the Scene Collection,

226
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
you can see that the avatar

227
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
is imported as Armature

228
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:07,000
and the garment is imported as Armature.001.

229
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Select the Armature.001

230
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
under Null and,

231
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
while holding down Shift,

232
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
drag it downward.

233
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Since the transform of Armature.001

234
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
has changed,

235
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
select Armature.001,

236
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
then change the scale to 0.01

237
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
and rotation X to 0

238
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
in the transform on the bottom right.

239
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Delete the unnecessary Null

240
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
at the bottom.

241
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Select Armature.001

242
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
and rotation X to 0.01.

243
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Set the options as shown in the image

244
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
and proceed with Fix Model.

245
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Delete Body Mesh.

246
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
We'll remove the hidden body mesh

247
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
that is covered by the garment.

248
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Select the body.

249
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Switch to Edit Mode either

250
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
by clicking on Edit Mode in the top left

251
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
or pressing the Tab key.

252
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
If you want to select both sides at once,

253
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
press Alt plus Z

254
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
to switch to X-Ray mode.

255
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Then,

256
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
drag to select the parts of the body

257
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
you want to delete.

258
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Afterward,

259
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
choose Delete,

260
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Vertices to remove the mesh.

261
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Adjust the viewport mode if necessary.

262
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Merge Avatar.

263
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
If deleting the hidden body mesh

264
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
is complete,

265
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
let's merge the Avatar

266
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
and Garment into one.

267
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Select the Armature first

268
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
and Control-Select Armature.001.

269
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Then,

270
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
in the CATS add-on,

271
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Custom Model Creation,

272
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
choose the options as shown in the image

273
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
and click Merge Armature.

274
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
This will combine the two bones into one.

275
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:08,000
If the Avatar and Garment are merged,

276
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
let's check for any errors

277
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
by adjusting the pose.

278
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Select the bone,

279
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
then change to Pose Mode

280
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
either by switching to it

281
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
in the upper right corner

282
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
or by pressing Control-Tab key.

283
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Choose the bone you want to move

284
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
and check if both the Avatar

285
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
and Garment move smoothly when rotated.

286
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Select the bone you want to move

287
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
and check if both the Avatar

288
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
and Garment move smoothly when rotated.

289
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Eye Tracking and Lip Sync for the Avatar

290
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
can also be configured in the CATS add-on.

291
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
You can set up the Eye Tracking

292
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,000
in the Eye Tracking tab

293
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
and Lip Sync in the By Seams tab.

294
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Export FBX.

295
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
When all the tasks are completed in Blender,

296
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
export it in FBX format.

297
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Click on the Export Model

298
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
at the top of the CATS add-on.

299
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Specify the file name and path,

300
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
change the path mode on the right to

301
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Copy and click Export FBX to save.

302
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Custom Model Setup in Unity

303
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
In Unity, we'll proceed with Avatar settings,

304
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
shader configurations,

305
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
format changes

306
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:36,000
and VRChat upload tasks.

307
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Install

308
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
To install Unity,

309
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
please refer to the official

310
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
VRChat Guide link at the top

311
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
and install Unity Hub

312
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
along with the recommended version

313
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
2022.3.6

314
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
as of March 2024.

315
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
To set up VRChat Avatars in Unity,

316
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
you need to install the Creator Companion

317
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
provided by VRChat.

318
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Please visit the link at the top,

319
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
download and install it.

320
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Once the installation is complete,

321
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
choose Create New Project

322
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:14,000
and select Unity 2022 Avatar Project.

323
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Set the project name and storage location,

324
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
then click the Create Project button

325
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
at the bottom.

326
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,000
In the next step,

327
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
click Open Project to open the project.

328
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
If the installation is successful,

329
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
you will see the VRChat SDK

330
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
tab in the top toolbar.

331
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Importing and setting

332
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Now, let's import the custom model file.

333
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
In the bottom asset window,

334
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,000
right-click,

335
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Create,

336
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Folder to create a model folder.

337
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Drag and drop the FBX file exported from Blender

338
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
into the folder you just created.

339
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
If you drag and drop the FBX file

340
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
from the asset window to the hierarchy window

341
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
in the top left,

342
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
the avatar will appear in the scene.

343
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
If the avatar isn't visible in the scene,

344
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
press F to focus on the avatar

345
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
and adjust its visibility.

346
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Select the model FBX in the asset window,

347
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
then click on the Rig tab

348
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
in the top right inspector window.

349
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Change the animation type to Humanoid

350
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
and click the Apply button.

351
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Click the Configure button to check

352
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
for any issues if it is activated,

353
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
then click Done.

354
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Material and Shader

355
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Now, let's proceed to set up the shader.

356
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Select the model FBX file

357
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
in the bottom asset window,

358
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
then click on the Materials tab

359
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
in the top right inspector window.

360
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Choose Extract Textures

361
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
and select the same folder

362
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
to load the textures.

363
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
If a notification appears,

364
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
click Fix Now.

365
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Follow the same steps for

366
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Extract Materials below.

367
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
This will generate materials

368
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
and they will automatically be applied

369
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
to the model.

370
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Next, let's make adjustments

371
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
to the texture and material settings

372
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
for the transparent parts of the avatar.

373
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Select the imported texture image,

374
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
activate Alpha is Transparency

375
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
in the right inspector window

376
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
and click Apply below.

377
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Choose the generated materials,

378
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,000
then change the rendering mode to Cutout

379
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
in the right inspector window.

380
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
We will be using the Poyomi Tune Shader

381
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
as it is the preferred shader

382
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
among VRChat users.

383
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Please download it from the provided link.

384
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Once you've downloaded the file,

385
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
simply drag and drop it

386
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
into the asset folder.

387
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Go back to the model folder,

388
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
select the material and

389
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
in the inspector window,

390
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:02,000
change the shader to the Poyomi Tune Shader.

391
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
After the change,

392
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
in the rendering menu,

393
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,000
set Cull to Off to enable

394
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
double-sided rendering of the garment.

395
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
You can adjust other detailed properties

396
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,000
in the inspector window

397
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
to create the desired material.

398
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
To upload an avatar to VRChat,

399
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
avatar descriptor configuration

400
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
is essential.

401
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Select Model FBX

402
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
from the hierarchy on the top left,

403
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
then click Add Component

404
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
on the right to add

405
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
a VRC avatar descriptor.

406
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Click Edit in the view

407
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
to adjust the viewpoint through the gizmo,

408
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
ensuring it fits between the eyes.

409
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Once adjustments are complete,

410
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
click the Return button.

411
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
You can also set up lip sync

412
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
and iLook here.

413
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
If you select Auto Detect,

414
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
it will automatically recognize lip sync

415
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
and when lip sync is enabled,

416
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
the avatar's mouth will

417
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
synchronize with the user's speech

418
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
when using the microphone in the VRChat.

419
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Enabling the iLook

420
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
allows users to blink their eyes

421
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
or move their pupils within VRChat.

422
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
To set up iLook,

423
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
click Enable and apply

424
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
the same values as shown in the image

425
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
for both eyes and eyelids.

426
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
To set up iLook,

427
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
click Enable and apply

428
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
the same values as shown in the image

429
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
for both eyes and eyelids.

430
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Uploading and playing to VRChat

431
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Uploading and playing to VRChat

432
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
VRChat Upload

433
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Alright, we've completed

434
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
all the necessary setups in Unity.

435
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Now, let's open the SDK window

436
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
to input avatar information

437
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
and run necessary validation checks

438
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
for uploading to VRChat.

439
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Navigate to the VRChat SDK

440
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,000
tab at the top of the menu

441
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
and click on Show Control Panel.

442
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Once the VRChat SDK

443
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
window appears, please

444
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,000
log in.

445
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
Confirm that the desired

446
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,000
avatar is properly

447
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,000
selected in the Selected Avatars

448
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,000
section. Enter the necessary

449
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
information in the Avatar Info

450
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
section.

451
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
You can set the visibility to

452
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Private or Public under Visibility.

453
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,000
In the Thumbnail tab,

454
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:28,000
you can insert a custom thumbnail

455
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,000
you've created or capture

456
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
an image from Unity's scene.

457
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Set it to your preferred thumbnail.

458
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
In the Validation section,

459
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
press the Auto Fix button to

460
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
address any issues automatically.

461
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Once the configuration is complete,

462
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,000
go to the Build tab,

463
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
check the Online Publishing checkbox

464
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
and click Build and Publish.

465
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Once the upload is finished,

466
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
click on the See it on the

467
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
VRChat website button

468
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
to verify if the upload

469
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
was successful on the

470
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
VRChat website.

471
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
If you encounter any difficulties

472
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
at this stage, please check

473
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
your VRChat account rating.

474
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
To register a new avatar

475
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
on VRChat, you must attain

476
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
at least the rank of New User.

477
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Play in VRChat.

478
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Alright, let's now check

479
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
if both the Avatar and the

480
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Iron Man garments have been

481
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
successfully uploaded and functioned

482
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
correctly within VRChat.

483
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
To play on your desktop,

484
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
please open VRChat through Steam.

485
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
If you don't have Steam installed,

486
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
proceed to download and install

487
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
it from the link provided at the top.

488
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
After logging in,

489
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:46,000
navigate to the home that is

490
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
the default space in VRChat.

491
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Use the WASD keys

492
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,000
to move towards the mirror.

493
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Press the ESC key

494
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
to open the launch pad

495
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,000
then select the uploaded avatar

496
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
under Avatar, Uploaded.

497
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Click the Change into Avatar

498
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:04,000
button to switch avatars.

499
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Close the launch pad

500
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,000
by pressing ESC again

501
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
and move around in front of

502
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,000
the mirror to see everything

503
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,000
is functioning properly.

504
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Press the spacebar to jump

505
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,000
and press C to crouch.

506
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
If there are any issues,

507
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
please return to the problematic areas

508
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
and

509
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
make the necessary corrections.

510
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
If everything is good to go,

511
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
enjoy playing with the avatar

512
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,000
you've created in VRChat.

513
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
So far, we have covered the process

514
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
of creating VRChat garments

515
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,000
using Everywhere in this tutorial.

516
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Thank you for watching

517
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,000
and if you have any questions,

518
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,000
please let us know through the comments.

